A||||8||Jay-ID||ZZ430 or Fast Burn 385 SBC with TPI||||5||
Z||000000||Jay-ID||12-14-2001||05:55 AM||||I've heard rumors that a ZZ430 with TPI can't be installed in a fiero.  Anyone know if this is true?  I'd really prefer the ZZ430 to the ZZ4.<BR>Here's some info for those unfamiliar with the ZZ430: <A HREF="http://www.goautocenter.com/fast_burn__zz430.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.goautocenter.com/fast_burn__zz430.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Archie||12-14-2001||06:52 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay-ID:<BR><B>I've heard rumors that a ZZ430 with TPI can't be installed in a fiero.  Anyone know if this is true?  I'd really prefer the ZZ430 to the ZZ4.<BR> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Both the 385 FastBurn and the 430 FastBurn engines use the new GM FastBurn (FB)heads. You cannot use a TPI intake manifold on those heads.<P>The FB heads are advertized as being "double drilled" (for both bolt patterns). The problem is that even though the TPI manifold will bolt onto the FB heads, the intake ports in the heads are so large that with the intake manifold on the engine you can still see down into the intake ports.<P>So an engine with the FastBurn heads cannot be used in ANY car with GM TPI.<P>Hope this helps<P>Archie<P>------------------<BR>Just how fast do you want to go?||||reg||1
Z||000002||pherder||12-14-2001||08:08 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B> Both the 385 FastBurn and the 430 FastBurn engines use the new GM FastBurn (FB)heads. You cannot use a TPI intake manifold on those heads.<P>The FB heads are advertized as being "double drilled" (for both bolt patterns). The problem is that even though the TPI manifold will bolt onto the FB heads, the intake ports in the heads are so large that with the intake manifold on the engine you can still see down into the intake ports.<P>So an engine with the FastBurn heads cannot be used in ANY car with GM TPI.<P>Hope this helps<P>Archie<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR><B><FONT SIZE="3">NEWS UPDATE!!!!</FONT></B><P>Scoggin-Dickey Parts Center releases a TPI manifold that fits the Vortec heads!!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.sdpc2000.com/cart.asp?action=prod_detail&catid=1460&pid=13740" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sdpc2000.com/cart.asp?action=prod_detail&catid=1460&pid=13740</A> <P>So you <B>CAN</B> use the ZZ430 or Fastburn 383 with the TPI system!<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Patrick's Dad||12-14-2001||10:05 AM||||The question was, can this be placed within the confines of the Fiero? Based on what I saw at the site, this is a "run of the mill" Small Block, so yes, it can be done. What mods you'll need in electronic control, etc. are not my specialty.<P>Check <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>  or ask him here on the forum.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||12-14-2001||01:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by pherder:<BR><B>  <BR>[b]<FONT SIZE="3">NEWS UPDATE!!!!</FONT></B><P>Scoggin-Dickey Parts Center releases a TPI manifold that fits the Vortec heads!!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.sdpc2000.com/cart.asp?action=prod_detail&catid=1460&pid=13740" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sdpc2000.com/cart.asp?action=prod_detail&catid=1460&pid=13740</A> <P>So you <B>CAN</B> use the ZZ430 or Fastburn 383 with the TPI system!<P>Paul<P>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 12-14-2001).][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, but aren't the Fast Burn heads different than the Vortec heads?  I believe the ZZ4 has Aluminum Vortec heads already, and that can be used with TPI.<P>Archie?  ||||reg||5
Z||000005||pherder||12-14-2001||02:02 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B> Yes, but aren't the Fast Burn heads different than the Vortec heads?  I believe the ZZ4 has Aluminum Vortec heads already, and that can be used with TPI.<P>Archie?  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>They are both "fast burn" heads ... the MAIN difference is the material ... cast iron/aluminum.  The valve sizes are different also.  (2.00/1.94 intake and 1.55/1.50 exhaust)<P>The ZZ4 has the TPI Aluminum heads ... otherwise known as Corvette L98 Heads NOT the Vortec/FB heads.<P>Paul<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 12-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay-ID||12-14-2001||06:03 PM||||Archie, thanks for the fast reply.  I'm certainly new to this forum but judging by the archives, your contribution has been amazing.  I've been visiting your site for months and dreaming about a V8 Fino.  I plan on ordering a V8 Fiero from you this summer.<BR>In regards to your post and others, I should probably rephrase my question.  Can a non-carbureted ZZ430 be installed in a Fiero? The tpi/vortec intake baseplates look interesting but the hp figures are worse than a stock ZZ4.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Jimmy||12-14-2001||11:20 PM||||If you bolt vortec heads up to a ZZ4 you will gain HP, somewhere around 15 more horse.  I wouldn't do that however as I would want to save weight with aluminum heads instead of gaining 15 HP.  <P>Jim<BR>87 GT T-TOP V8<BR>87 GT ||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||12-14-2001||11:45 PM||||Best damned heads out there, PEROID.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.araoengineering.com/images/gryhed.jpg"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.araoengineering.com/images/ARAODY4.gif"> <P>Daaaaaaamn!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.araoengineering.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.araoengineering.com/</A> <P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
